---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const canonical = 'https://allaboutjerky.com/about/';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About Cole Mercer | allaboutjerky.com"
  description="Meet Cole Mercer — a Bozeman, Montana pitmaster with 15+ years making homemade beef jerky. The story behind allaboutjerky.com."
  canonical={canonical}
>

  <!-- HERO -->
  <div class="about-hero">
    <img
      src="/images/cole-mercer-smoker.jpg"
      alt="Cole Mercer at his smoker in Bozeman, Montana"
      class="about-hero__img"
      width="1344"
      height="768"
      loading="eager"
    />
    <div class="about-hero__overlay">
      <h1 class="about-hero__title">About Cole Mercer</h1>
      <p class="about-hero__subtitle">Bozeman, Montana · Pitmaster · Jerky Obsessive</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- CONTENT -->
  <div class="about-content">

    <!-- INTRO GRID: photo + text -->
    <div class="about-intro-grid">
      <div>
        <img
          src="/images/cole-mercer.jpg"
          alt="Cole Mercer holding beef jerky strips near his smoker"
          class="about-author-photo"
          width="280"
          height="350"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="about-intro-text">
        <span class="eyebrow">The Pitmaster Behind the Recipes</span>
        <h2 style="margin-top:0; color: var(--clr-text); font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3.5vw, 2.4rem);">Hi, I'm Cole.</h2>
        <p class="tagline">I've been making beef jerky longer than some people have owned a smartphone.</p>
        <p>I'm a 39-year-old jerky maker and pitmaster based in Bozeman, Montana. I didn't grow up with a culinary school degree or a Food Network contract. I grew up with a grandfather who made the best jerky I've ever tasted — and who never once wrote down a recipe.</p>
        <p>That's where this site started: my obsession with reverse-engineering what he did by feel, and learning the science behind why it works.</p>
        <div class="about-signature">— Cole Mercer</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- STATS -->
    <div class="about-facts">
      <div class="about-fact">
        <span class="about-fact__number">15+</span>
        <p class="about-fact__label">Years making jerky</p>
      </div>
      <div class="about-fact">
        <span class="about-fact__number">300+</span>
        <p class="about-fact__label">Batches tested</p>
      </div>
      <div class="about-fact">
        <span class="about-fact__number">5</span>
        <p class="about-fact__label">Drying methods mastered</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- STORY -->
    <h2>My Grandfather's Smokehouse</h2>
    <p>Every October, my grandfather would disappear into his little smokehouse behind the house. He'd come out hours later with strips of venison and elk jerky that smelled like hickory smoke and black pepper. He never used a thermometer. He never set a timer. He just knew.</p>

    <p>When he passed, there was no recipe box. No notes. Just my memory of the smell and the texture and the way he'd hold a strip up to the light to check it. I was 24 years old, and I decided I was going to figure it out.</p>

    <p>Fifteen years and somewhere north of 300 batches later, I think I've got a pretty good handle on it. I've made jerky in a $40 Nesco dehydrator, in a $2,000 Traeger pellet smoker, in a regular oven with a wooden spoon propping the door open, and in an air fryer at 11pm because I didn't want to wait until morning.</p>

    <h2>The Philosophy: Jerky Is a Craft</h2>
    <p>Great jerky isn't just dried meat. It's a balance of tenderness and chew, smoke and spice, sweet and salt. It's patient work — the marinade needs time, the drying needs airflow, and the finished product needs to rest before you taste it.</p>

    <p>I built allaboutjerky.com because I couldn't find a single resource that treated jerky the way I think it deserves to be treated: as a craft, not a food hack. Most jerky content online is vague, contradictory, or just wrong. ("Dehydrate at whatever temperature until it's done" is not a recipe. It's a prayer.)</p>

    <p>Every recipe on this site has been made in my own kitchen — or backyard, or smoker shed — multiple times. The temperatures are exact. The times are tested. The cuts are recommended for a reason. When I say "160°F for 4–6 hours in a dehydrator," I mean it.</p>

    <h2>What I Make</h2>
    <p>My flavor wheelhouse leans bold and savory, with occasional detours into sweet territory:</p>

    <div class="about-flavors">
      <span>Bourbon Maple</span>
      <span>Chipotle Honey</span>
      <span>Cracked Black Pepper</span>
      <span>Garlic Habanero</span>
      <span>Sweet Teriyaki</span>
      <span>Classic Peppered</span>
      <span>Korean BBQ</span>
      <span>Dr Pepper Glaze</span>
    </div>

    <p>I've made jerky from eye of round, top round, flank steak, London broil, ground beef, venison, elk, and one very memorable batch of wild boar that I'd rather not talk about. The point is: if it's lean, I've probably tried to turn it into jerky.</p>

    <h2>When I'm Not Making Jerky</h2>
    <p>I spend a lot of time exploring the ranches and farms around Bozeman, looking for interesting local beef and game. Montana has some of the best cattle country in the world, and I take ingredient quality seriously — great jerky starts with great meat, long before the marinade.</p>

    <p>I also advise a few local butcher shops on jerky seasoning blends, which is exactly as unglamorous as it sounds but I love it.</p>

    <p>If you have a question about a recipe, a technique, or which cut of meat to use, reach out. I read every message.</p>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <div style="margin: 3rem 0; padding: 2rem; background: var(--clr-highlight); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); border: 1px solid var(--clr-border); text-align: center;">
      <h3 style="margin-top:0; font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 1.5rem;">Ready to make your first batch?</h3>
      <p style="color: var(--clr-muted); margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Start with the beginner guide — everything from choosing your cut to the bend test.</p>
      <div style="display: flex; gap: 1rem; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap;">
        <a href="/how-to-make-beef-jerky/" class="btn-primary">Beginner Guide →</a>
        <a href="/" class="btn-outline">Browse All Recipes</a>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

</BaseLayout>
